protocol_basis:
Every field here is a published protocol fact, not a design choice. The system message is exactly f"{system_prompt}

## Available Tools:
{tool_lines}": task_instruction_template carries the adapter's hard-coded default system_prompt verbatim (its four sentences separated by single spaces) plus the fixed header, and task_instruction_fill renders tool_lines through format_tools_compact -- one "- {signature}: {description}" line per tools_registry.csv row, sorted by tool_name under plain Python string order, nothing else from the registry. The user turn carries the audio first and then the fixed sentence "Convert this voice command to a tool call.", which is the adapter's own content-part order. No native tools list is sent: the adapter never passes tools= to apply_chat_template and IGNORES the per-call tools argument, the per-item functions field and the per-item instruction field.
